solutions.latex:
The graph of $y=f(x)$ is increasing for $x\in(-\infty,0)$, decreasing for $x\in(0,\infty)$, stationary at $x=0$, and $y\to1$ as $x\to\pm\infty$.

Hence $y=f'(x)$ must be above the $x$-axis for $x<0$, below the $x$-axis for $x>0$, have an $x$-intercept at $x=0$, and $f'(x)\to0$ as $x\to\pm\infty$.

\exfigure{156_q11e_s1}
